OL,3,AChina's growth accelerates as AI export
OL,4,Aboom outweighs domestic weakness
OL,5,
OL,6,FChina's economic growth picked up in
OL,7,Fthe three months to the end of
OL,8,FSeptember, rebounding from a three-year
OL,9,Flow as the artificial intelligence (AI)
OL,10,Fboom helped boost exports.
OL,12,FThe world's second largest economy grew
OL,13,Fby 4.5% in the third quarter, up from
OL,14,F4.3% in the previous period but below
OL,15,Fthe 5% expansion recorded from January
OL,16,Fto March, according to official Chinese
OL,17,Fdata.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/18
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1792378459
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AChina's growth accelerates as AI export
OL,4,Aboom outweighs domestic weakness
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe latest figure is at the bottom end
OL,7,Fof Beijing's annual growth target of
OL,8,F4.5%-5%, which analysts have said gives
OL,9,Fpolicymakers room to address the
OL,10,Fcountry's economic challenges.
OL,12,FExports have helped offset weak
OL,13,Fspending at home, but global trade
OL,14,Ftensions and uncertainty over AI
OL,15,Finvestments are clouding its outlook.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/18
